# The Celestial Tower (the tower where Pokémon are laid to rest): a slow tolling bell tune in A minor over a hushed choir, a
# low string line, a harp that rises and falls like breath, and a single timpani stroke every second bar. The tower plays
# the same by day and by night. Original composition for this game (plan 22 · U7, part a).
title Celestial Tower
tempo 66
meter 4/4
reverb 0.5
night none

track lead bell vol=0.66 pan=0.1 rev=0.5
  L o5 e2 a2 | o5 c2 f2 | o5 e2 g2 | o5 d2 g2 |
  o5 a2. e4 | o5 f2. c4 | o5 d2 f2 | o5 g+2 e2 |
  o6 c2 o5 a2 | o5 f2 a2 | o6 e2 c2 | o5 b2 o6 d2 |
  o6 e2. c4 | o5 a2. f4 | o5 f2 d2 | o5 e1 |

track pad choir vol=0.42 pan=-0.2 rev=0.5
  L o4 (a >c e)1 | o4 (f a >c)1 | o4 (c e g)1 | o4 (g b >d)1 |
  o4 (a >c e)1 | o4 (f a >c)1 | o4 (d f a)1 | o4 (e g+ b)1 |
  o4 (a >c e)1 | o4 (f a >c)1 | o4 (c e g)1 | o4 (g b >d)1 |
  o4 (a >c e)1 | o4 (f a >c)1 | o4 (d f a)1 | o4 (e g+ b)1 |

